#FREED###ENTER#


A1. What do reformers tread upon? ~ HEELS
A5. What works best when tired? ~ WHEEL
A9. What letters mean "that is?" ~ IE
A10. What are we advised to investigate before we act? ~ LEAP
A12. What is a go-getter? ~ DOER
A13. Name a conjunction. ~ OR
A15. What is a pretty girl who goes to a dance unaccompanied? ~ ALONE
A16. What is bad—carried to the superlative degree? ~ WORST
A18. What are Spanish swells? ~ DONS
A20. What are always found running between in hills? ~ DALES
A22. What is the best thing to take when about to fall in love? ~ TRIP
A24. What is a filling-station in England? ~ INN
A25. What means nothing at all? ~ NIL
A26. Give a part of the verb to be. ~ ARE
A27. What are high fliers? ~ ACES
A29. What were the pointed debates of the Middle Ages? ~ DUELS
A31. What is often on the house? ~ LIEN
A32. What is a person who knows his onions? ~ EXPERT
A34. What holds the low-speed record of the World? ~ SNAILS
A36. What is always epochal? ~ ERA
A37. What lubricated certain political machinery recently? ~ OIL
A38. What is the net made of in which men are caught? (Plural.) ~ CHARMS
A41. What makes the mare go? ~ FORAGE
A44. What is a bird bill? ~ BEAK
A45. What is a soak? ~ STEEP
A47. What was the old original homestead? ~ CAVE
A49. What should waiters learn to do correctly? ~ ADD
A50. What are all eggs? ~ OVA
A51. Name a movie star the boys all like. ~ MIX
A52. What can be told by the collar it wears? ~ BEER
A54. What kind of plant is much used in salads? ~ CRESS
A56. What often masquerades as gold? ~ GILT
A57. What is the skin all women love to touch? ~ SABLE
A59. What is a polite word for stolen? ~ TAKEN
A61. Name a little adverb. ~ SO
A63. What do authors want their books to be? ~ READ
A64. What is always found around the animals? ~ SKIN
A65. Who is the last word in domestic relations? ~ MA
A66. What should the slaves be? (Yes, we know this is 1927.) ~ FREED
A67. What do politicians do to get on the inside? ~ ENTER

D1. Name a purely masculine word. ~ HE
D2. What measures equal 1¼ yards? ~ ELLS
D3. What is the fifth sign of the Zodiac? ~ LEO
D4. What did Lawrence of Arabia have a lot of? ~ SAND
D5. What does Dumb-Dora think a lawyer does at court? ~ WOOS
D6. Name a pronoun. ~ HER
D7. What word means formerly? ~ ERST
D8. Name an exclamation—rather poetical. ~ LO
D9. Where is Kipling's "cleaner, greener land?" ~ INDIA
D11. What is raised in the South and downed in the circus? ~ PEANUT
D12. What does a President rarely ever do in the White House? ~ DWELLS
D14. What is the best thing green apples do? ~ RIPEN
D15. What is it "to take possession of?" ~ ANNEX
D17. What was the Indian's highway?" ~ TRAIL
D19. What adverb means "formerly?" ~ ONCE
D21. Name a kind of bedtime story. ~ LIE
D23. What little things are indicative of angry people? ~ IRES
D28. What is it dumb people never do? ~ SPEAK
D29. What are little drinks? ~ DRAMS
D30. What do blue noses do? ~ SNOOP
D31. Name a pinkish, purplish flower. ~ LILAC
D33. What is it always a mistake to do? ~ ERR
D35. What does a flat tire need—and usually get? ~ AIR
D38. What word means yield? ~ CEDE
D39. What was the underworld of ancient Greece? ~ HADES
D40. Where does a wise man keep his wet goods? ~ STORED
D41. What are always gratifying to doughboys? ~ FEASTS
D42. What was Oliver Twist? ~ GAMIN
D43. What is never good? ~ EVIL
D44. What midnight broadcasters are hard to tune out? ~ BABES
D46. Who handed out the first applesauce? ~ EVE
D48. Who is a Movie hero's double? ~ EXTRA
D53. What are dry Congressmen who will not drink? ~ RARE
D54. What is every well-dressed person? ~ CLAD
D55. What liquor is made from rice? ~ SAKE
D56. Who is not quite a gentleman? ~ GENT
D58. Who is always buzzing around? ~ BEE
D60. What are domestic relations? ~ KIN
D62. Name a preposition. ~ OF
D65. Name an abbreviation used only in connection with men. ~ MR


